<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:43:13Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-all" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-all" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Why the era of cheap government debt is over</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0de2aced0f2f29db69f0d97432fb05bd23c91d2d6d9d8b3b937abae13ae17f47</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272--435550125c87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-the-era-of-cheap-government-debt-is-over/a-79259272?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US debt has topped $40 trillion. How risky is the growing debt burden, and will investors keep funding Washington's deficits?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>US allies in Asia alarmed as think tank calls for pullback</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:663a17e7c5d2234b373071bbfc93251faa4d6514559d32a9e4c88f9c6bdc3afd</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554--5c1e9b8e70e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-allies-in-asia-alarmed-as-think-tank-calls-for-pullback/a-79275554?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Analysts warn that a US withdrawal from the western Pacific, as recently suggested by a think tank, would weaken deterrence and strengthen China's position.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: 'Woman, Life, Freedom' lives on despite war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f26099c45d6875aa14343b82410b5299d6a226feffa5b954b0d482a0c25d5ea1</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-woman-life-freedom-lives-on-despite-war/a-79276123--cc6a8d951841.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-woman-life-freedom-lives-on-despite-war/a-79276123?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The death of Jina Mahsa Amini triggered a resistance movement in Iran. Four years later, the Iranian regime endures — but so does the legacy of the "Woman, Life, Freedom" protests.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bangladesh court sentences 7 Hasina allies to death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:179349eb5629835b459146bdc2579a2e4fdb63f8bc8829096fe5cc893f6f829d</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:25Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T12:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bangladesh-court-sentences-7-hasina-allies-to-death/a-79276131--93bfc83fec03.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bangladesh-court-sentences-7-hasina-allies-to-death/a-79276131?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The latest verdict brings to 22 the number of death sentences handed down in cases stemming from the 2024 uprising that ended Sheikh Hasina's 15-year rule.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Berlin election driven by radical ideas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:81ca6893fa254ae276f635d0632d4072f48287d5fbdeed96682e8efee98dda18</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/berlin-election-driven-by-radical-ideas/a-79256516--15d2b53f017a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/berlin-election-driven-by-radical-ideas/a-79256516?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The results of the Berlin election are as hard to predict as ever. Three parties are vying for first place, including the socialist Left Party and the far-right AfD. But one issue is most important to Berliners.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Police find arms depot near highway</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84e1d45c66f30539719f60be26d3da7707d994a2ed6e3e14134668e2165c95e1</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-find-arms-depot-near-highway/live-79273324--57b471e5aa19.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-find-arms-depot-near-highway/live-79273324?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police have found a stash of rifles, pistols and other firearms near a road in the western state of Rhineland-Palatinate. Meanwhile, Defense Minister Pistorius is off to Washington for talks with his US counterpart.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>SPD governor campaigns as one-woman bulwark against AfD</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bb6b26b6b2f03d8020907b890fdd3b12a38bc8210ea685ad03e65c57ecef972</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spd-governor-campaigns-as-one-woman-bulwark-against-afd/a-79264225--0135376188de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spd-governor-campaigns-as-one-woman-bulwark-against-afd/a-79264225?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuela Schwesig, of the center-left SPD, has governed the state of Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, on the Baltic Sea coast, since 2017. Ahead of this weekend's election, she is campaigning against the nationalist AfD.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>US confirms it has weapons in space</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80b3c68de047ae1ab8cd2ca16395fe47af461da26a2268a7cbd526648ec23cea</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-confirms-it-has-weapons-in-space/a-79268894--7b3b13289f4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-confirms-it-has-weapons-in-space/a-79268894?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US Space Force justified the weapons deployment by citing its two biggest geopolitical rivals — Russia and China. Beijing responded by urging Washington to "stop preparing for war" in outer space.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>NATO jets shoot down drone over Lithuania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2d75fa5226d2bda8066faf03885d1b001ed17a891a5b30ff24550b404513df0</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T10:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nato-jets-shoot-down-drone-over-lithuania/a-79267975--4d3ef910416c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nato-jets-shoot-down-drone-over-lithuania/a-79267975?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The drone, which is believed to have entered Lithuanian airspace from Belarus, was shot down by an Italian fighter jet in between the cities of Vilnius and Kaunas. There have been no reports of casualties or damage.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian warship fires flares at Danish helicopter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83d0c9934369110a4dad75633968dc4fae67f16f0b4a8a163e1498e488be3bd2</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T10:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-warship-fires-flares-at-danish-helicopter/a-79270510--158a6506bc4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-warship-fires-flares-at-danish-helicopter/a-79270510?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Denmark has summoned Russia's ambassador over a Baltic Sea encounter that Copenhagen says is part of an increasingly aggressive pattern of Russian behavior.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China tightens travel rules over tech security</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7719e950404682cce3a2336b9f3ba4c9fface1bbdc759a728be7fb3fd40fc89e</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-tightens-travel-rules-over-tech-security/a-79270217--ad2e766020cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-tightens-travel-rules-over-tech-security/a-79270217?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Beijing says the new rules, which could also apply to foreign and Taiwanese nationals, are aimed at safeguarding "national security."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Netherlands: Suspected sabotage disrupts train services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5c95fa3abad2dcc14a762eeabb44f411c790b0f4733b2e144f0a4352706d003f</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600--a0c80c1ea5f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/netherlands-suspected-sabotage-disrupts-train-services/a-79269600?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A major outage has hit parts of the Dutch railway system after objects were found placed across lines, authorities say. The company responsible for rail infrastructure says it suspects deliberate wrongdoing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: Meta to report child abuse cases to law enforcement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1646bb4935eb7aa8a8a44eb89b5c2fb83e420dfe6db8c24f25a78e7c31bf88b9</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-meta-to-report-child-abuse-cases-to-law-enforcement/live-79268751--04c495e204f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-meta-to-report-child-abuse-cases-to-law-enforcement/live-79268751?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tech giant Meta will now directly report child safety-related cases to India's cybercrime portal, according to media reports. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why top AI researchers are warning about human extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e064b7d1d5fc1879b5b346a8a762e8a22fab5b5fa9035768374e6c8fb0bd941</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-top-ai-researchers-are-warning-about-human-extinction/a-79263146--1de1f181920f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-top-ai-researchers-are-warning-about-human-extinction/a-79263146?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Could artificial intelligence pose an existential threat to humanity? Some leading researchers are warning against an unregulated race toward AI superintelligence.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>El Salvador court hands down first life sentence for femicide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8dd6a5a994843e4b7cfb611fcf435c463e367aa4bbfea17d6252944c8c839e91</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/el-salvador-court-hands-down-first-life-sentence-for-femicide/a-79268746--3332ccb66681.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/el-salvador-court-hands-down-first-life-sentence-for-femicide/a-79268746?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The landmark conviction comes 42 days after the killing of a woman in Santa Ana who prosecutors said was stalked and harassed by her neighbor.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran and US: Two countries and the pistachio between them</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b03e988187b9762ccd1470000f27750d4e61877a460767da31c1132df1578878</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-and-us-two-countries-and-the-pistachio-between-them/a-79224310--28756f33fc8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-and-us-two-countries-and-the-pistachio-between-them/a-79224310?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The pistachios sold across the United States have a surprising history: California's trees trace their roots to Iran. Now, both regions face the same threat — their farmland is sinking as groundwater disappears.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>Europe launches two climate observation satellites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6140ccff371dc127877f5b26d94cefce2237f38b1446bebc6580ee6aba11a325</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:43:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705--7858649e62ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/europe-launches-two-climate-observation-satellites/a-79268705?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Space Agency has put two satellites into orbit to take a closer look at the impact of climate change. One of them will focus particularly on plant life.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US scraps greenhouse gas rules for power plants</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:356b682182fc67a8407c3a0cd52c600bd79dd6dfbe985b556630fac4650e9948</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:43:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T05:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-scraps-greenhouse-gas-rules-for-power-plants/a-79268393--51c0df356c7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-scraps-greenhouse-gas-rules-for-power-plants/a-79268393?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Environmental Protection Agency said it was repealing Biden-era limits on emissions made by power plants, in the "largest power sector deregulation action ever."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US Supreme Court denies Trump bid to restrict mail-in ballots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbcc506222812e264623be05f5b11cfe391235f33cf45e0f956ad0780d178577</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T01:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-supreme-court-denies-trump-bid-to-restrict-mail-in-ballots/a-79267854--d0b3a2fd6f50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-supreme-court-denies-trump-bid-to-restrict-mail-in-ballots/a-79267854?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The court said election officials do not have sufficient time to implement the rule before the November midterms. Trump has argued, without providing evidence, that the system is vulnerable to fraud.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz urges CDU discipline as pressure grows</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ee08925db227777d7a6260a9c7d2a78363aad8af2ecd81af7eb2734044476234</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T00:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-urges-cdu-discipline-as-pressure-grows/live-79256902--10c6578e951f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-urges-cdu-discipline-as-pressure-grows/live-79256902?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz has urged his party to stay disciplined as pressure grows over his leadership. Meanwhile, Germany's homeownership rate has fallen to its lowest level in 20 years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU seeks Arctic strategy amid growing power rivalry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:386e5aa3d9e13d4e75f768e22cac6a7a5b3d7c3919fc6501eeddebb87e30bd40</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:43:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-arctic-strategy-amid-growing-power-rivalry/a-79266739--8da58b1eb0cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-arctic-strategy-amid-growing-power-rivalry/a-79266739?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's aggression, Trump's threats against Greenland and the race for critical raw materials are pushing the Arctic to the top of Europe's agenda.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, Russia set for new round of US-mediated talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9904ac08df0e8a5be8aec347e0fc3b270abbd7dc92c700f6ac71d03c2430a2d6</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T18:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-set-for-new-round-of-us-mediated-talks/a-79261147--0cf6c10eaa61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-russia-set-for-new-round-of-us-mediated-talks/a-79261147?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New trilateral talks between Ukraine, Russia and the US could begin in October, according to Kyiv and Moscow. Few expect a breakthrough, but Ukraine is seeking a partial de-escalation to help it get through the winter.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trump seeks halt to energy attacks by both Russia, Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:205d9efc969f1c89b50c058adc2e928cafdf4f19de2f6bdbd1fa341259702e5a</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T17:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-seeks-halt-to-energy-attacks-by-both-russia-ukraine/a-79265774--121a884cf5a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-seeks-halt-to-energy-attacks-by-both-russia-ukraine/a-79265774?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump, under fire for record US diesel prices, claims Russia and Ukraine have agreed to stop striking energy targets. Russia said nothing; Ukraine said "we expect specifics from our partners" on any such move.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Women's Basketball World Cup: Can Germany harness a boom?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa9082828a05c0842da47e04d8be6ecbe545e5411c82ec0667974c99baf62d7f</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T15:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602--77d972e02866.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany thrilled fans at the Women's Basketball World Cup. But even if this sparked a boom in the women's game, the infrastructure simply isn't ready for it.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's richest man Dangote's IPO out of reach in Nigeria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cad65b8da9136d5333f1d4238a5c94ba45067de97129c5eb0cf8f5a29dac42ad</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:43:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-richest-man-dangote-s-ipo-out-of-reach-in-nigeria/a-79263398--03e0d1756308.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-richest-man-dangote-s-ipo-out-of-reach-in-nigeria/a-79263398?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dangote seeks $1.6 billion from investors to finance a $14.3 billion expansion and thus double the oil refinery's capacity. The offer could give millions of Nigerians a stake in the company. But who can truly afford it?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Far-right AfD puts pressure on German aid to Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d79b75952102568cfca19f7a55314d31951f42e6a668c7d66a25c599ed22beac</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:43:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/far-right-afd-puts-pressure-on-german-aid-to-ukraine/a-79257524--80d6e129ea25.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/far-right-afd-puts-pressure-on-german-aid-to-ukraine/a-79257524?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emboldened by its win in Saxony-Anhalt, the far-right Alternative for Germany wants the government to change its Ukraine and Russia policies. Berlin is staying the course, but support is fading — especially in the east.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>The Crusades: How a medieval holy war still shapes politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07e5a92400e25efe8f4dc55b0b2a6b8ffb5e80c459e6ffd091872b40ac6f94d5</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-crusades-how-a-medieval-holy-war-still-shapes-politics/a-79203784--8fa07b173177.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-crusades-how-a-medieval-holy-war-still-shapes-politics/a-79203784?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 1095, the Catholic Church launched the Crusades: wars that left millions dead and whose legacy still shapes political and ideological conflicts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>EU leaders urge unity after Russian strike on train</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae6f0c7f977f33a34263e8d81f2f097d4fe8821a2aabc943c10438ad31627814</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-urge-unity-after-russian-strike-on-train/a-79259807--826cde282d81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-urge-unity-after-russian-strike-on-train/a-79259807?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's drone attack on a train near the Ukraine-Poland border has triggered EU calls to up support for Kyiv. Allies of Ukraine should show they "are not scared," said the bloc's top diplomat, Kaja Kallas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can Iran replace sea trade with land routes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:035a14e43b672d9e1126a2957672c4d85353dbb0286b31d5f6d23ba02b5a49f9</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T07:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-iran-replace-sea-trade-with-land-routes/a-79211179--9748aa6cdc36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-iran-replace-sea-trade-with-land-routes/a-79211179?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran is shifting trade toward northern ports and land routes as its southern shipping faces a US blockade. Analysts say the corridors can keep essential goods moving, but cannot replace maritime trade.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>In cosmopolitan Berlin, elections still closed to foreigners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dccb9f9734f264d88d10a936efa5cfe4d374a58234188bc434affaceb5c4bb44</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579--2c7a3b66c58f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter of Berlin residents will have no say in the German capital's city-state election because they lack citizenship. That's the highest proportion of residents excluded from the election yet, and many are unhappy.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Merz's CDU comes out on top in Lower Saxony polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38e34bffc59a261c0128e6988a9f27fa1cd09b0a178fdd431b5d1e00d2dcdefe</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T06:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-merz-s-cdu-comes-out-on-top-in-lower-saxony-polls/a-79254724--04c4d8ef8565.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-merz-s-cdu-comes-out-on-top-in-lower-saxony-polls/a-79254724?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Christian Democrats have emerged as the strongest party following local elections in the state of Lower Saxony. The vote was closely watched as an indicator of the strength of the far-right AfD, which came in third.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Zverev wins US Open in golden year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff6b7cf0c46b72d48ced9079f3afd7284d12b86b66fd6d3882215f527f77f188</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T22:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706--d962ccd6a0c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-zverev-wins-us-open-in-golden-year/a-79212706?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Alexander Zverev has won the US Open for the first time, defeating Ben Shelton in the final. It is Zverev's second Grand Slam win of 2026 after a long wait for his first title, but controversy still hangs over him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Russians on the Goethe-Institut: 'Hostage to politics'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6a36ae927fb32f5fc28364755e942d84eba4e992cae7c0113bd1fe8d93ef627</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T11:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936--8619b68c7998.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canceled language exams, disrupted plans to study in Germany and the disappearance of an important cultural link: DW users shared how the closure of Germany's Goethe-Institut in Russia has affected their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A Romani artist in Hungary reclaims his identity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:732362ee7162a43ea61b6d9a397d9ac97d3c4be0eb6aece6bb13b19915844624</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-romani-artist-in-hungary-reclaims-his-identity/a-79247266--3fed9cef9147.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-romani-artist-in-hungary-reclaims-his-identity/a-79247266?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Norbert Olah is an artist. He's also Romani. For a long time, he avoided making his ethnic background a theme of his art for fear of being pigeonholed. Then it became his focus.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why are European banks moving gold out of United States?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38bee224cf6eaeaa8535e3ced72bfe7098fce4a101e6cf57e940d9fc5ffb27fa</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T15:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-are-european-banks-moving-gold-out-of-united-states/a-79213013--320ff1551fa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-are-european-banks-moving-gold-out-of-united-states/a-79213013?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Netherlands and France have moved their gold out of US vaults. Part of the reason is fears about the reliability of the US, but equally important is the need to keep gold closer to home in the event of a crisis.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Corals as climate archive: Are El Nino events intensifying?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c430979a780de293d13934157af26311f2c5cc2b5b2c606de6de494dbd479569</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T08:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/corals-as-climate-archive-are-el-nino-events-intensifying/a-79243425--ac4752671640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/corals-as-climate-archive-are-el-nino-events-intensifying/a-79243425?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Records show that El Nino events have been frequent and often extreme over the past few decades. Is this normal? Or is it the result of climate change? Corals can give us a clear indication.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's drone war comes to Moldova and Romania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9787a2279a179ef6d6c7ffbcf244854514ce11582d213df3174262da16e76c2</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T06:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-s-drone-war-comes-to-moldova-and-romania/a-79239591--15076a5f335b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-s-drone-war-comes-to-moldova-and-romania/a-79239591?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Incursions by Russian drones into Moldovan and Romanian airspace are increasingly common. This week the Ukrainian president's plane was stopped from taking off from Chisinau. Observers suspect the attacks are deliberate.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>DW exclusive: Zelenskyy offers to meet Putin at G20 in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea26387588a41bd1b1ac0344e8e0e81fb14f7c99ba100bae19d9aa3403156057</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T05:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-exclusive-zelenskyy-offers-to-meet-putin-at-g20-in-miami/a-79241703--3aacfd955f7d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-exclusive-zelenskyy-offers-to-meet-putin-at-g20-in-miami/a-79241703?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In an interview with DW, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said his country was in a strong position to negotiate and offered to meet Vladimir Putin in Miami.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India looks to steer BRICS away from anti-Western turn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e580c44fde12d615b40bcc18d822138371b8e7404bdf02cecb0d2fb6791afa4</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234--e9a076e9f28e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-looks-to-steer-brics-away-from-anti-western-turn/a-79195234?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The BRICS summit 2026 takes place in Delhi this weekend. Unlike last year, Putin and Xi are expected to attend. Can India keep the expanded bloc united?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Turks in Germany anxious after AfD wins in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:746cd29469352129e179ecdfa330bc2580843367c2bb6daa0fdc0fc028b6c200</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764--9bdd69d84853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party's win in Saxony-Anhalt has alarmed people of Turkish origin in eastern states. Will workers and business owners abandon the increasingly AfD-friendly region for the more welcoming west?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>The 'end of an era' as Goethe-Institut in Russia closes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cda291875f6c2a46ade2bbe8b4c383d86d6ade670f648ba50137a0876ce33fe</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-end-of-an-era-as-goethe-institut-in-russia-closes/a-79224321--189393464061.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-end-of-an-era-as-goethe-institut-in-russia-closes/a-79224321?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Goethe-Institut was one of the last German institutions still operating in Russia. However, following Moscow's decision to close its offices, all employees will have to stop working by September 13.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Magyar vs. Moscow: Hungary toughens stance toward Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dff8755f3be8c40bd47aca1eaab97673cea3d97ff36fe92ca7aab0999eae235a</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T08:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/magyar-vs-moscow-hungary-toughens-stance-toward-russia/a-79223424--a42f60a005da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/magyar-vs-moscow-hungary-toughens-stance-toward-russia/a-79223424?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Peter Magyar has abruptly ended the era of his predecessor's warm relations with Russia: Hungary has expelled 10 Russian diplomats. The Kremlin is considering halting gas supplies in response.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany sets its sights on Russia's shadow fleet</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b5109c787cc08ba554b8f4004e96b59edd7816ec01a8408a8ed0227429e878f</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T05:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-sets-its-sights-on-russia-s-shadow-fleet/a-79211123--786b113b7d97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-sets-its-sights-on-russia-s-shadow-fleet/a-79211123?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German government wants to follow other EU countries and take more decisive action against Russia's shadow fleet, accusing it of helping Moscow evade sanctions and carry out acts of sabotage.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Cyberattack in Berlin: 1.4 million files on the dark web</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4388b950055a1230f4efc19ae24f45d385b57d549229b6e9df7cd6305e55df69</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T16:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cyberattack-in-berlin-1-4-million-files-on-the-dark-web/a-79220829--b03a66e17cd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cyberattack-in-berlin-1-4-million-files-on-the-dark-web/a-79220829?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Shortly before Berlin's state parliamentary election, the hacker group Rhysida stole data, tried to extort the Berlin Senate and published the data on the dark web after their attempt failed.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How Celine Dion became a pop culture icon across generations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:964cb4c7cca8253a4b57e0d0ab74c882687519bc92f7f41dc6e4de399599a308</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-celine-dion-became-a-pop-culture-icon-across-generations/a-79213779--40db204d1ea8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-celine-dion-became-a-pop-culture-icon-across-generations/a-79213779?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the global star kicks off her anticipated Paris residency, here's how Celine Dion managed to gain younger followers while keeping her loyal older fans.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Are electric cars really bad for the environment?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba3fb08068497a129d10ac68e41b6b2c6e129112e67a7339d0933678b6e304f4</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/are-electric-cars-really-bad-for-the-environment/a-79213336--69d71b67dca0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/are-electric-cars-really-bad-for-the-environment/a-79213336?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some German politicians are calling for a delay to the EU plan to phase out gas-powered vehicles, saying cars must be judged on the entire carbon footprint. But the full picture still says EVs are more climate friendly.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia, the conflicted EU candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b11895ce754cf564aa25dc73db4d112c2162722ba15fa7069c3a4d07a65b6bf</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T05:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774--0a94078faf3f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-the-conflicted-eu-candidate/a-79203774?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On paper, Belgrade has pursued EU membership for years. But accession has long been stalled. The hero's farewell given to war criminal Mladic exposed just how far Serbia has alienated itself from Europe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How Belarusians still find hope in a silenced country</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe04df071ec273eb7b43e99b0bec812bda101c8dd2056084942713c406ed641a</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-belarusians-still-find-hope-in-a-silenced-country/a-79127285--d234556fa838.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-belarusians-still-find-hope-in-a-silenced-country/a-79127285?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The documentary "Letters from the Silenced Country" depicts the ongoing repression under the authoritarian regime. Director Andrei Kutsila talked to DW ahead of the film's Venice premiere.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Why we're still looking for dark matter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf47a75ba81ba5fb71c497333717787a767b5bd25fd4f610a8f259f8d4800cfe</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T13:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-we-re-still-looking-for-dark-matter/a-79189395--3bfbe0fa2ce3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-we-re-still-looking-for-dark-matter/a-79189395?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When physicists said they may have spotted evidence of dark matter almost 100 years after it was proposed as a theory, the internet lit up. Here's why we're searching for the thing that holds everything else together.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>LIV Golf in financial turmoil: What's next for the sport?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92ea12f4014f736ba4bb80c2656c18588db9ccbfde804e6a6baef58a5c95a745</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T11:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/liv-golf-in-financial-turmoil-what-s-next-for-the-sport/a-79199569--378367d5fd0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/liv-golf-in-financial-turmoil-what-s-next-for-the-sport/a-79199569?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Six months after Saudi Arabia pulled funding from the breakaway organization, LIV Golf have filed for bankruptcy protection. Several of the world's best players signed on to LIV, so where does that leave golf?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Conspiracy theories can provide answers but not peace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d98b7cd3a979365d93dd5d583c4791bcb2c2835588d11975bbe3b63590ceb8a</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/conspiracy-theories-can-provide-answers-but-not-peace/a-79022756--b464ce7f771c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/conspiracy-theories-can-provide-answers-but-not-peace/a-79022756?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Twenty-five years after 9/11, conspiracy theories about the terrorist attacks persist. But even as an attempt to make sense of a tragedy, psychologists say the benefit in conspiracy ideation or belief is short-lived.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>The billion-euro trade driving Europe's eels to extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e93dc7ef565d6fcb4de6a729308b5872c2ef5f86cf218ca6b73264a001c6d725</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145--e574ad564b10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Traffickers are making big bucks smuggling millions of critically endangered eels across continents, using suitcases on planes and legal loopholes to deliver them to dinnerplates. Where are the smuggling hotspots?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>The Bayeux Tapestry in London: What's behind the hype?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d63e626ed513c625b72d5719a1aea43dbda95e79204dac323c0a00adc3457310</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-bayeux-tapestry-in-london-what-s-behind-the-hype/a-78488629--9a9477f8929c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-bayeux-tapestry-in-london-what-s-behind-the-hype/a-78488629?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The exhibition of the Bayeux Tapestry at the British Museum is eagerly anticipated across the UK, as the medieval masterpiece is considered by many to be a symbol of the country's identity.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>EU sports commissioner says FIFA is 'damaging to football'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac30fa0f9046896efa9f09af15289baeb5b7d211a053bf433328152dc01578bb</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T07:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-sports-commissioner-says-fifa-is-damaging-to-football/a-79193424--c7a4bd30a298.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-sports-commissioner-says-fifa-is-damaging-to-football/a-79193424?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Speaking to DW, EU Commissioner Glenn Micallef hit out at world football's governing body over its "poor governance."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Putin rejects mobilization rumors, many Russians unconvinced</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ac8832ee7b2094ca7a76a31f