freezing-in-women-s-football-choice-or-pressure/a-79145259?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's football federation is set to join a handful of clubs in paying for female players to freeze their eggs. Experts have welfare concerns.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f267f960be171ff835f0650454dda850757ff0c5d1bd7a81befc6ea3edd40583</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Nicaragua challenges German arms exports to Israel at ICJ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0912ce7654a433366a603e1b21e466b75d3941b38bce256b765f7eab1a0d397</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044--315737afbbdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has asked the International Court of Justice to dismiss the case on jurisdiction grounds. It also said its arms exports to Israel were documented, published, and subject to more stringent checks than most.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Germany wakes up to 'unsettling' AfD victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:897cf9c8a66a382a8ff7692cd48d0b5b1fd6223b19e44b1e3ab9adc619d3c169</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-germany-wakes-up-to-unsettling-afd-victory/live-78754934--2d9595de9f5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-germany-wakes-up-to-unsettling-afd-victory/live-78754934?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) party won the Saxony-Anhalt state election but without an absolute majority in parliament. Other European nations were wrestling with the impact of the results. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AfD wants to form a government in Saxony-Anhalt — but how?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ff8ed59a54b399ec601aea715cea5200311de32e63842c88991b1f5f47cb9b8</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-the-afd-form-a-government-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79107331--72d013c68919.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-wants-to-form-a-government-in-saxony-anhalt-but-how/a-79107331?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following its record election success, the far-right Alternative for Germany aims to form a government. What options does it have without the absolute majority?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>War criminal Ratko Mladic buried with military honors in Belgrade, Serbia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aaf5c4a2ef0340d441527ad40a65c2ff0d96e0046720053aa236e9cb3aa0ce40</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T15:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/war-criminal-ratko-mladic-buried-with-military-honors-in-belgrade-serbia/a-79148678--c4979d87a1d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/war-criminal-ratko-mladic-buried-with-military-honors-in-belgrade-serbia/a-79148678?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ratko Mladic, the former Bosnian Serb commander convicted of genocide in Srebrenica, has been buried in Belgrade. The funeral, broadcast live on TV, comes just days before President Vucic is expected to call an election.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Chancellor Merz says AfD result 'changes all of Germany'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08837fe80c1a7e99e512afae5b5d77de41e086412c970e2e1bef6b6d09fd59db</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T15:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/chancellor-merz-says-afd-result-changes-all-of-germany/a-79150560--fdb0b7e42c28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/chancellor-merz-says-afd-result-changes-all-of-germany/a-79150560?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A visibly shaken but also determined Friedrich Merz spoke in Berlin about the AfD's election victory in Saxony-Anhalt and the CDU's bitter defeat. He insisted on sticking to his reforms.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys Witkoff and Kushner hold Ukraine talks after meeting Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:875a09f451a71fbe736831a1c9aa6c530272da97b89add53dd40b917ac37fe69</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T22:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779--687b66a14041.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner held talks with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Kyiv, seeking to revive efforts to end the war. But the latest diplomatic push seems to have produced no breakthrough.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Digesting the AfD's landmark election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e6840c9c1bb0e84bd9f1a318de6f2bee81013b27fa85d9bcd6b06ee046f4b71</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T21:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-digesting-the-afd-s-landmark-election-win/a-79103981--03f4036eaf84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-digesting-the-afd-s-landmark-election-win/a-79103981?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With well over 40% for the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD), Saxony-Anhalt has witnessed a landmark election night. DW's reporters were on the ground.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Election fraud claims spread in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1316a7fa4a7262ae93bbef0abf47f49b72e83c140051dfbfa915ea9c22b16cf</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T19:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-election-fraud-claims-spread-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79093254--984abe33c1c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-election-fraud-claims-spread-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79093254?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">False and misleading claims are raising questions about the integrity of the election in Saxony-Anhalt. DW Fact Check takes a closer look.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany set to feel the impact of Saxony-Anhalt's AfD win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe7371774a96b652607011fe9b8e6d35fc2390674955349b437d71b735d9859a</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T18:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-set-to-feel-the-impact-of-saxony-anhalt-s-afd-win/a-78874569--97dfb85b6e8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-set-to-feel-the-impact-of-saxony-anhalt-s-afd-win/a-78874569?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The state election could have major consequences for Germany's government. Pollsters cite dissatisfaction with Merz as one reason for the CDU's poor showing.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt election: Why the AfD is so strong</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf0e5117819eccde3c6cf678ef52cebe784209d64906838302a2d6868815dc00</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T18:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-election-why-the-afd-is-so-strong/a-78482588--f7f12ed5af71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-election-why-the-afd-is-so-strong/a-78482588?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD has emerged as the strongest party in Germany's eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt by a wide margin. What is driving support for the far right in this predominantly rural eastern German state?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, Kosovo unite against ticks carrying deadly virus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:636202d49e0bedaa4637c2f44920729f32cb0bb9112fef1f14c212d77624d0ce</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223--2c267f5d11c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has high-security labs while Kosovo has Hyalomma ticks and experience with the deadly Crimean-Congo hemorrhagic fever. Working together, German and Kosovar scientists are fighting the disease and its vectors.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany plans anti-drone shield over Leipzig attack — report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b0af34a8f087f7fc7eda2f27bff12953f2a561dfda6851ee2b358481b634e39d</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-plans-anti-drone-shield-over-leipzig-attack-report/a-79052604--572615382eed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-plans-anti-drone-shield-over-leipzig-attack-report/a-79052604?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several German cities will receive rapidly deployable units capable of defending against drone strikes on critical infrastructure, according to Bild am Sonntag newspaper.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary begins hunt for corrupt regime's billions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3001864a4bcf8379e6df62c7bf359b1d195c39b9d7f5dead0a448b33a638f149</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T05:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-begins-hunt-for-corrupt-regime-s-billions/a-79047176--0dd17c410606.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-begins-hunt-for-corrupt-regime-s-billions/a-79047176?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's new prime minister promised he would recover billions stolen or diverted by the previous administration. A new "super authority" is about to begin that work. Its success or failure will have a big impact.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Croatia: Toxic waste protest draws tens of thousands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d890657ac3e2c2d734114d2c493b6d08506c748e2b3b8bace2c0bbdb68a6c9af</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T17:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228--9dec1bdce80c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/croatia-toxic-waste-protest-draws-tens-of-thousands/a-79049228?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Zagreb demonstrators demanded that the government come up with a plan to clear illegal toxic waste in 20 days. Prime Minister Plenkovic has promised to tackle the issue.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: From emigration to immigration destination</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37de42eb13ff2f9ef2c68ba41b09026b6b10842cd38821edaf29830b6ffcc07c</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T08:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541--ac3bd047b864.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-from-emigration-to-immigration-destination/a-78805541?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Migration is a sensitive topic in Germany, with public debate dominated by the fear of uncontrolled immigration. But over two centuries, millions of Germans emigrated in search of a better life.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Thousands march at Saxony-Anhalt rallies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3d812954d08d281ed9d92d5ec6ab92f7ec7178d0eef9d5da910210e0167a2c2</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-march-at-saxony-anhalt-rallies/live-79041302--28cda5652dc8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-march-at-saxony-anhalt-rallies/live-79041302?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of Saxony-Anhalt's state election on Sunday, a democracy festival by civil society groups has been held in Magdeburg. The far-right AfD organized its final campaign rally in the state capital.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What would an AfD government in Saxony-Anhalt really mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:685a044eccf3414c616c9105db3dd5f1e626c48e9b8c7bee272c9b30bb1314bc</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T06:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-would-an-afd-government-in-saxony-anhalt-really-mean/a-78869947--261ff10619b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-would-an-afd-government-in-saxony-anhalt-really-mean/a-78869947?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Detention centers for deportation, mandatory work for asylum-seekers, vigilante groups — the AfD wants to drastically overhaul Saxony-Anhalt. What does the party have planned?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Outrage as Maltese tycoon acquitted in journalist's murder</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cdc13d509a2ef7d1fbf9ce5882279a7f4679a6cec16529c535b956446c70325</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008--2a5e65f2e4f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/outrage-as-maltese-tycoon-acquitted-in-journalist-s-murder/a-79027008?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Maltese businessman Yorgen Fenech has been found not guilty of complicity to murder journalist Daphne Caruana Galizia. Almost nine years after the attack, the question of who ordered her death remains unanswered.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>In Saxony-Anhalt election, small parties will be kingmakers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2103c98349bcac1a9cc4ee71568a8363d6ed4651922e4c4caea5a54471c1d677</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-saxony-anhalt-election-small-parties-will-be-kingmakers/a-78482460--43a765f0394e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-saxony-anhalt-election-small-parties-will-be-kingmakers/a-78482460?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD has good odds of winning an absolute majority in Saxony-Anhalt's parliament this state election, enabling them to govern alone. It all depends on whether other parties make the cut.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>The hidden environmental cost of AI data centers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fef6864c1f0a05a5dd72da998d06b902feb61765169271ccf7eb4684c09d97a7</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T11:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-environmental-cost-of-ai-data-centers/a-78789889--5e00024ffa87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-hidden-environmental-cost-of-ai-data-centers/a-78789889?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As data centers multiply to meet AI demand, they're straining power grids, draining water supplies and reshaping the land and air around them.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia: How the funeral of Ratko Mladic is dividing a nation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c7ad5c9aedf4c478e7f3d1343573c0a17fb5571d31fc405c371f87fbd86005e</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-how-the-funeral-of-ratko-mladic-is-dividing-a-nation/a-78948890--47086bf0a8c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-how-the-funeral-of-ratko-mladic-is-dividing-a-nation/a-78948890?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the Serbian government leaves the decision about Ratko Mladic's funeral arrangements to his family, international pressure on the country is mounting. How do Serbs feel about the matter?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Is Saxony-Anhalt's economy really struggling?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:872c8b5d00b2883870a4f9e7dcc4c26e02b62b9b132fcaffb805a36066841918</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-saxony-anhalt-s-economy-really-struggling/a-78867143--acfa7a18352e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-is-saxony-anhalt-s-economy-really-struggling/a-78867143?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's far-right AfD party has long claimed that the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt has been left behind. Is that really the case? A closer look at the data offers some interesting insights.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Why North Korea's women's football team is so good</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:715d6f7258f8df1a8e1f5c3393de46f9d4fb9f39ae0fa3c5e09e526d6d6d52db</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-women-s-football-team-is-so-good/a-70313505--6b31ccb5ebf0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-north-korea-s-women-s-football-team-is-so-good/a-70313505?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea's young footballers enter the U-20 World Cup in Poland as defending champions — the 2024 title was their third. Why is the isolated state so good at the game?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Beethoven Festival evokes a sense of home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1de6fb61cd63bbb001a1a813f88a36100ca9afee5ed7d77fc598ac45fc183651</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997--9bbbc99c220c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The motto of this year's classical music festival in Bonn is "Home/At Home," featuring musicians from diverse cultures presenting pieces from their homelands.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>How Volkswagen's huge workforce became a costly burden</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73f7d61a4b4b55d28b564087441cf8a198e7e0fbaf8cc09ee7282098f4bedd82</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-volkswagen-s-huge-workforce-became-a-costly-burden/a-77766154--6b1e762393dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-volkswagen-s-huge-workforce-became-a-costly-burden/a-77766154?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The struggling German carmaker plans to cut up to 100,000 jobs from its 630,000-strong workforce. How did VW's headcount get so bloated, and will the cuts be enough to survive the Chinese EV onslaught?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Norway seizes Russian ship in Svalbard to compensate Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4dd3e3137d2550980ff5bda746d20681d8644f555c55dd6c5f49b010eb7faff4</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/norway-seizes-russian-ship-in-svalbard-to-compensate-ukraine/a-78889005--08f506bc071c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/norway-seizes-russian-ship-in-svalbard-to-compensate-ukraine/a-78889005?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Norway have seized a Russian ship, the Professor Molchanov, on a court order sought and obtained by Naftogaz in Ukraine. Russia has protested the move, which stems from its refusal to pay Naftogaz damages.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is Germany's economic slump finally over?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:060e39ed183dae8384b7793e16f732fe0f84dc25e3c5d43bae56ecbdab26238c</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T12:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-economic-slump-finally-over/a-78815447--a101d614d4d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-germany-s-economic-slump-finally-over/a-78815447?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite a slew of negative headlines, the German economy has posted its best figures in years. There are reasons for optimism, but structural issues remain.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Austria women ice hockey team fight for future generations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0619cad458eeede17189c12ae722d19cb813295bfbfd87a972f178341de86d13</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T15:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578--3801f62b822d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/austria-women-ice-hockey-team-fight-for-future-generations/a-78771578?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Austria are getting ready for their first Women's Ice Hockey World Championship. But preparations have been overshadowed by a dispute about conditions, pay and getting men's cast-off kit. A solution now looks in sight.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football: Anyomi, London City and the German exodus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:106796ee7d25e6a1a9397b459c541b478cf332854fc6aaa690ba6d6ec43b2358</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T07:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-anyomi-london-city-and-the-german-exodus/a-78446131--1f6d62473b8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-anyomi-london-city-and-the-german-exodus/a-78446131?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nicole Anyomi has joined Alexia Putellas and other star names in signing for the ambitious English club London City Lionesses. The Germany winger told DW England is a better place to develop her game than back home.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Can communities be protected from melting glaciers?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3408c1c4502dd036b12c1f33a9ed53fbd009d861d77a1f1c783b93e5c7ffb72</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-glaciers-melt-can-communities-be-protected/a-78615775--a898d3259825.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-communities-be-protected-from-melting-glaciers/a-78615775?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rising temperatures are increasing the risk of floods and avalanches in mountain regions. The disaster in Nepal and Tibet shows the urgent need for solutions, and the tools that could help save lives.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Can new Apple CEO John Ternus fix the tech giant's AI woes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fe1ba89416464a3c8a5fee6a96138a03a77bdacf3e3ecf8159efc2a3c84e152</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-fix-the-tech-giant-s-ai-woes/a-78575898--ec9f6d3fb1f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-new-apple-ceo-john-ternus-fix-the-tech-giant-s-ai-woes/a-78575898?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">John Ternus is just the third Apple CEO in 30 years. His primary challenge is to correct the company's faltering AI strategy to preserve its position as a big tech leader.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>At Venice Film Festival, politics take center stage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b2c38a7f403256d937c936e55bfd6261524f3050b781401cc31f72257a315cd</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T14:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/at-venice-film-festival-politics-take-center-stage/a-78493761--39adfe1f0702.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/at-venice-film-festival-politics-take-center-stage/a-78493761?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With works about Gaza, Ukraine and Elon Musk, political cinema is in the spotlight at the 2026 Venice Film Festival.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Canada's Carney holds firm against Trump tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab3dec435c782dffaaadc6b20a89f5d0253fb8e149f04ac3038af37578a386f4</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-s-carney-holds-firm-against-trump-tariffs/a-78542754--4ad6d16c6985.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-s-carney-holds-firm-against-trump-tariffs/a-78542754?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canada is facing new US import penalties after Prime Minister Mark Carney refused to match US tariffs on China. Other countries are watching as the Trump trade clash turns into a fight over economic sovereignty.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Inside the sea cucumber smuggling boom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:324f0d971671a0d4358c4611b540b98a796387acf894ae3a3fe69b7a188a5f53</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/inside-the-sea-cucumber-smuggling-boom/a-78005662--ad829420fb34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/inside-the-sea-cucumber-smuggling-boom/a-78005662?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quiet multimillion‑dollar black market is exploding across the Indian Ocean, driven by one unlikely animal: the sea cucumber.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Ailing Djokovic 'despised' every moment of US Open defeat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffba8d841f61d58a2b66fa9d2d28f6a91344f8fae5ba4dbf5dcfb33eb9ba77a1</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ailing-djokovic-despised-every-moment-of-us-open-defeat/a-78572187--352c93994800.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ailing-djokovic-despised-every-moment-of-us-open-defeat/a-78572187?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Novak Djokovic has exited in the first round of a Grand Slam for the first time in over two decades. Could time — or an unknown health condition — be catching up with the Serbian tennis legend?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU wants drones to spray pesticides, but it could backfire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fc9548ff55a8484c2094c617d5311d197e114a0e1f895568ab44246ecb68dbb</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T15:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-wants-drones-to-spray-pesticides-but-it-could-backfire/a-78557154--b8aa3ba6b326.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-wants-drones-to-spray-pesticides-but-it-could-backfire/a-78557154?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants to lift a decades-old ban on spraying pesticides from the air, allowing drones to be used for greater precision. But experts warn the plan could lead to even more pesticides being used in agriculture.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>This extremely successful author polarizes German readers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:965f8afb050fe3a052954d20be25e6b6e7b3c1a33d119f7ac220bef9fde1e79f</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452--1ca180b39c00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-extremely-successful-author-polarizes-german-readers/a-78500452?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">She's young and she says what she thinks: Caroline Wahl is topping Germany's bestseller lists with her novels. But she has also faced a public backlash.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>What 'The Odyssey' can teach us about climate chaos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a854814ea7d83b7511e8864f8880737aa446cb278e68248cb2f594a48eb5489</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T12:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-odyssey-can-teach-us-about-climate-chaos/a-78545407--d5adc3479f14.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-odyssey-can-teach-us-about-climate-chaos/a-78545407?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bronze Age collapse may have started with a water crisis. The droughts of today raise the unsettling question of whether it could happen again.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Influential humanists: These are the winners of the Goethe Medal 2026</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1780b337c606ef40a09545195e3074d853388e2c18b53b9be9bc6062467d3ad8</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T12:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/influential-humanists-these-are-the-winners-of-the-goethe-medal-2026/a-78497975--2a003f94b40a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/influential-humanists-these-are-the-winners-of-the-goethe-medal-2026/a-78497975?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The prestigious German cultural award recognizes the artistic work and commitment to cultural dialogue of Arvo Pärt, Anita Raja and Prodromos Tsinikoris.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's military wants to recruit tech-savvy gamers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1868aa9be3c34c82ca316049878b27047ed85659cff03a803998ad1b2f0940af</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T10:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462--a4ab0409cda1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-military-wants-to-recruit-tech-savvy-gamers/a-78536462?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bundeswehr has been a fixture at Gamescom, Cologne's video game trade fair, for years. But critics say military recruitment does not belong at an entertainment convention.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: Thieves steal Bronze Age gold in lightning raid on Villena Museum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf4839d8c5ecc0f96b0018cb25340753f1aabacee860c096c5afc06a3c08c52d</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T19:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-thieves-steal-bronze-age-gold-in-lightning-raid-on-villena-museum/a-78538027--71179a9fbd6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-thieves-steal-bronze-age-gold-in-lightning-raid-on-villena-museum/a-78538027?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One of the world's greatest Bronze Age gold collections has been swiped, almost in its entirety, from Villena Museum. A highly professional group of thieves were in and out in four minutes flat before the museum opened.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tragedy in Nepal: How do flash floods happen?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d345a9719468c1c00e9af17b44089c342194e2d7a295da142ba3b9384f4d5801</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T14:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tragedy-in-nepal-how-do-flash-floods-happen/a-78526421--1b448fe4e3c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tragedy-in-nepal-how-do-flash-floods-happen/a-78526421?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When flash floods sweep through the Himalayas, there is often little time to react. Scientists are working to understand the risks and improve early warning systems.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Andre Rankel named Germany's new men's ice hockey coach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93bbbadb50f0f6cb80470a066f4584f867f9939481d695bab3543f64c0eaf5e3</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/andre-rankel-named-germany-s-new-men-s-ice-hockey-coach/a-78532470--9672475007d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/andre-rankel-named-germany-s-new-men-s-ice-hockey-coach/a-78532470?maca=en-rss-en-all-1573-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's men's ice hockey team has appointed a new head coach following a string of dissappointing tournaments. He's two decades younger than the man he's replacing but he has no previous experience as a head coach.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>New study shows German football remains male-dominated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5638d23fcd02ab4461f7b151a4758f2bdc66e36563d597d41963035c6bf267b</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:16Z